<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.6.2: Interpreting Negative Exponents in Exponential Growth</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01343</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.6.2: Interpreting Negative Exponents in Exponential Growth</md:title>
    <md:uuid>69578409-9dfa-4034-8d6e-d0257bb2b381</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>A marine biologist estimates that a structure of coral has a volume of 1,200 cubic centimeters and that its volume
  doubles each year.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/915e980323c039f033c1086572a5d1f032cef8c3"/></media></figure></para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Write an equation of the form \(y=a\cdot b^t\) representing the relationship, where \(t\) is time in
        years since the coral was measured and \(y\) is volume of coral in cubic centimeters. (You need to figure
        out what numbers \(a\) and \(b\) are in this situation.)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.
    </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(y=1,200\cdot 2^t\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the volume of the coral when \(t\) is 5, 1, 0, –1, and –2. Note that when \(t = -1\), this
    represents one year before the marine biologist made the original estimate.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Time (years)</entry>
      <entry>5</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>-1</entry>
      <entry>-2</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Volume of Coral (cubic centimeters)</entry>
      <entry>a.____
      </entry>
      <entry>b.____
      </entry>
      <entry>c.____
      </entry>
      <entry>d.____
      </entry>
      <entry>e.____
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="485289d3-90ab-487d-ba23-6eb8a3238bf3" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="58888de2-7d9b-405d-a5bb-e1757fd262c3" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="3800">
    <problem>
      <para> Enter the volume of coral when t = 5. Do not enter commas in your answer. </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3800 cubic centimeters</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="48eecec1-7ae0-48d7-8d2d-912f221f88f8" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2400">
    <problem>
      <para> Enter the volume of coral when t = 1. Do not enter commas in your answer. </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 2400 cubic centimeters</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="ec7943f4-d9f7-430c-86f7-b965ddc0b967" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="1200">
    <problem>
      <para> Enter the volume of coral when t = 0. Do not enter commas in your answer. </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 1200 cubic centimeters</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="d325a246-3666-4e89-87ff-f46f511a3cb8" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="600">
    <problem>
      <para> Enter the volume of coral when t = -1. Do not enter commas in your answer. </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 600 cubic centimeters</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="839cb86e-da3a-45fc-9279-ca3b5bc704a5" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="300">
    <problem>
      <para> Enter the volume of coral when t = -2. Do not enter commas in your answer. </para>
        <para> Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 300 cubic centimeters</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What does it mean, in this situation, when \(t\) is –2?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> This represents the time 2 years before the scientist made the estimate of 1,200 cubic centimeters.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>In a certain year, the volume of the coral is 37.5 cubic centimeters. Which year is this? Be prepared to show
        your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(t\) is –5, or 5 years before the scientist made the estimate of 1,200 cubic centimeters.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
